 "response": "Volidrox's budget is now **$2082K**.\n\n**How I worked it out**\n\n1. **Only Finance Office budget entries count.** Messages from Vendor, Facilities, Legal, Engineering, Marketing, Sales, PMO and Operations do not change the budget. Finance Office notes that don't change the amount (receipts, audits, reminders, room moves) are also ignored.\n\n2. **Withdrawal chains were traced to their last step.** A withdrawal is in force unless it was itself withdrawn. Two examples:\n   - Update #0003 (\u2212$196K) still applies. #0004 withdrew it, but #0015 withdrew #0004. #0026 then withdrew #0015, but #0146 withdrew #0026. So #0015 stands, #0004 is cancelled, and #0003 applies.\n   - Update #0056 (\u2212$549K) still applies. Its chain runs #0069 \u2192 #0079 \u2192 #0162 \u2192 #0222 \u2192 #0553 \u2192 #0910. #0910 is not withdrawn, so #0553 is cancelled, #0222 stands, #0162 is cancelled, #0079 stands, #0069 is cancelled, and #0056 applies.\n\n3. **About 120 Finance Office updates end up withdrawn.** Among them are #0002, #0023, #0039, #0047, #0043, #0070, #0080 and #0077. Each surviving change was applied in record order, starting from the $2760K set in #0001.\n\n**Running total at a few checkpoints**\n\n| After record | Budget |\n|---|---|\n| #0001 | $2760K |\n| #0029 | $2862K |\n| #0127 | $4048K |\n| #0307 | $2405K |\n| #0580 | $2170K |\n| #0999 | $2028K |\n| #1307 | $3008K |\n| #1467 | $4022K |\n| #1597 (last budget change) | $2082K |\n\nANSWER: $2082K",
